From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 01:42:55 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: tabs fall asleep on their own, links copy clean,
 cookie banners hidden
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Auto-sleep: background tabs not used for a while (Settings > General:
  30 min / 1 h (default) / 4 h / Never) are discarded, all but the 5 used
  last. Never the open tab, split tabs, the Workbench, tabs playing,
  capturing, or with something typed (the same check as Put to Sleep), nor a
  pinned tab marked Keep Awake in its menu.
- Copy clean links (Settings > Advanced, on): Copy Link in tab and pinned
  menus, Copy Links, the site controls, the page's Copy Link Address, ⇧⌘C
  and the link button leave out tracking parameters; also Spotify's si and
  X's ref_src/ref_url, ttclid, srsltid, li_fat_id, epik.
- Hide cookie banners (Settings > Advanced, on): the EasyList Cookie List
  (CC BY 3.0) is downloaded at run time, kept in the user data folder and
  refreshed after 4 days; its element hiding rules go into every frame.
  --meridian-cookie-list=<file> for tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
